   "text": "I'm sorry about the wrong dish, Yusuf. When I checked Spice Route, I found an open incident on their account. Their supplier recalled a sauce batch used in their curries, and the recall covers orders placed between 5:00 and 7:00 PM tonight. Your order #K-6601 was placed at 6:58 PM, so it's one of them.\n\nBecause of that, I can't refund the Paneer makhani myself. Forkful's incident team compensates every affected order directly. I've passed your case to them (reference **ESC-700**), noting that you got Chicken makhani instead of Paneer makhani and asked for your money back. A specialist will contact you within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll decide.\n\n**Because of the recall, please don't eat the Chicken makhani, and to be safe, don't eat anything else from that order either.** I'm glad nobody has eaten it. If anyone eats something from that order and feels unwell, tell me right away so I can flag it as a food-safety issue.\n\nYou said a few things went wrong tonight. What happened with your other orders? I can see **#K-6602** (Spice Route) and **#K-6603** (Lotus Garden)."
